  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 AM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nAnother day of quiet weather returns to the Cowboy State today, as \nan area of high pressure shifts over eastern MT/WY and the western \nDakotas. The main impacts will be temperatures rising a few degrees \nabove normal in the Bighorn Basin and Natrona County and as high as \n13 degrees above normal over Johnson County today. Additionally, \nsouthwest winds with gusts up to 20 mph will occur from South Pass \nto eastern Johnson County this afternoon. \n\nA trough will move over the region on Friday, shifting the area of \nhigh pressure over the Dakotas and Upper Midwest. Very light rain \nshowers will be possible over Sweetwater County between 11Z and 20Z \nalong the tail end of the trough. West to southwest winds with gusts \nof 20 to 25 mph will impact most areas Friday afternoon in the wake \nof the trough. Otherwise, temperatures will return to more seasonal \nlevels. A broad ridge will then build over much of the Intermountain \nWest and extend over the Northern Rockies by Saturday keeping \nconditions dry. Above normal temperatures return to the Bighorn \nBasin and Johnson/Natrona counties Saturday, becoming more \nwidespread across the CWA on Sunday. A fast moving trough will pass \nover the northern half of the state Monday as the ridge folds over. \nThe flow pattern will be more zonal Monday and Tuesday, before \nanother ridge returns over the Northern Rockies Wednesday and \nremains in place Thursday. Conditions look to remain dry through the \nnext 7 days, apart from the aforementioned light showers possible \nFriday morning.",
